{
  "version": 1,
  "spec": "W23d AGT-14 captured HTTP exchanges: the cross-language test vectors. The server (schemas.HttpExchangeIn + services/http_exchange_redaction.py) and the Python SDK (client/http_capture.py) both run every case; the Java / JS / Go capture filters adopt this file when they capture. The vocabulary block is pinned equal to backend/app/services/http_exchange_vocab.py (and the redaction module's own constants) by backend/tests/test_payload_metrics_vocab_parity.py. Secret samples are real-looking and non-hex; none is a live credential. Grow it (new cases, new keys); never rewrite a case.",
  "conventions": [
    "Expand every generator spec (see generators) in input and expect before use.",
    "cases[].input is ONE exchange exactly as an SDK puts it on the wire (POST /api/v1/ingest results[].http_exchanges[] or POST /api/v1/stream/http-exchanges exchanges[]).",
    "cases[].expect is the exchange the server stores: every key present (method, url, endpoint, status, duration_ms, started_at, error, request, response, response_schema, response_schema_state, redaction_counts; each side {headers, body, body_truncated, body_bytes}); objects compare without regard to key order. null = the exchange is DROPPED (counted, never a 422 on the batch).",
    "Idempotence: redacting expect again yields expect, so the server's re-validation and an SDK's own first pass never change an already-redacted exchange.",
    "An SDK applies the same rules BEFORE it buffers anything; it may skip the BODY_STORED_MAX_BYTES cut (the server makes it) but no other rule. started_at is sent as ISO-8601 UTC with a Z suffix and stored as sent.",
    "The text pass (header values, query values, JSON string leaves and keys, non-JSON bodies, error): secret-named pairs (JSON_PAIR_RE / FORM_PAIR_RE whose key is secret-named), then TOKEN_SHAPES whole-token, then the server's redact_text patterns (credentials, JWTs, e-mail / phone / card / IPv4 shapes), then TOKEN_SHAPES again.",
    "Headers: at most HEADERS_MAX per side, sorted by name; a name in HEADER_DENYLIST or ending in a HEADER_SECRET_SUFFIXES entry (lower-cased, _ read as -) keeps its name and its value becomes [REDACTED]; a numeric value becomes its text; any other non-text value is skipped.",
    "The url: the userinfo password (or a bare userinfo) becomes [REDACTED]; a QUERY_DENYLIST name's value becomes [REDACTED], every other query value gets the text pass; the fragment is dropped; URL_MAX characters. The url is split by RFC 3986 appendix B (URL_PARTS_RE), never by a parser that refuses a bracket in the userinfo.",
    "The endpoint: an SDK-sent template keeps its segments (scheme, host, query stripped); otherwise the url's path with every segment matching ENDPOINT_ID_SEGMENT_RES replaced by {id}; ENDPOINT_MAX characters.",
    "Bodies: cut to BODY_WIRE_MAX_BYTES UTF-8 bytes first (state too_large, not parsed); JSON (no NaN / Infinity) is walked: a secret-named key's non-null, non-boolean value becomes [REDACTED], every list item is walked (no 100-item cut), a container deeper than JSON_DEPTH_MAX becomes [REDACTED], then re-serialised compact (the $json rule); other text gets the text pass; then cut to BODY_STORED_MAX_BYTES with TRUNCATION_MARKER ({omitted} = the bytes not stored). body_bytes = the size before the store cut.",
    "response_schema: top-level key -> JSON type of the redacted response body (state parsed only); a key outside FIELD_NAME_RE or beyond SCHEMA_KEYS_MAX is counted under UNNAMED_KEYS. A client-sent schema, state or redaction_counts is recomputed. redaction_counts counts the [REDACTED markers per part."
  ],
  "generators": [
    "{\"$repeat\": \"<text>\", \"times\": N} -> the text repeated N times.",
    "{\"$join\": [part, ...]} -> the parts (each expanded to a string) concatenated.",
    "{\"$list\": <value>, \"count\": N} -> a list of N copies of the expanded value.",
    "{\"$json\": <value>} -> the compact JSON text of the expanded value: \",\" and \":\" with no spaces, non-ASCII kept as is, keys in the order given.",
    "An object is a generator only when its keys are exactly those of one form above; every other object or array is walked and its members expanded."
  ],
  "vocabulary": {
    "EXCHANGES_PER_TEST_MAX": 20,
    "EXCHANGES_PER_RUN_MAX": 1000,
    "BODY_WIRE_MAX_BYTES": 65536,
    "BODY_STORED_MAX_BYTES": 16384,
    "TRUNCATION_MARKER": "…[truncated: {omitted} bytes not stored]",
    "HEADERS_MAX": 50,
    "HEADER_NAME_MAX": 128,
    "HEADER_VALUE_MAX": 2048,
    "URL_MAX": 2048,
    "ENDPOINT_MAX": 300,
    "METHOD_RE": "^[A-Z]{1,16}$",
    "SCHEMA_KEYS_MAX": 200,
    "FIELD_NAME_RE": "^[A-Za-z_$@][A-Za-z0-9_.$@:-]{0,119}$",
    "SCHEMA_STATES": [
      "parsed",
      "not_json",
      "empty",
      "too_large"
    ],
    "HEADER_DENYLIST": [
      "authorization",
      "proxy-authorization",
      "cookie",
      "set-cookie",
      "x-api-key",
      "api-key",
      "x-auth-token",
      "x-access-token",
      "x-csrf-token",
      "x-xsrf-token",
      "x-amz-security-token",
      "x-goog-api-key",
      "x-session-token",
      "private-token",
      "x-gitlab-token",
      "x-hub-signature",
      "x-hub-signature-256"
    ],
    "HEADER_SECRET_SUFFIXES": [
      "token",
      "secret",
      "password",
      "api-key",
      "apikey",
      "signature",
      "credential"
    ],
    "QUERY_DENYLIST": [
      "token",
      "access_token",
      "id_token",
      "refresh_token",
      "api_key",
      "apikey",
      "key",
      "code",
      "password",
      "secret",
      "client_secret",
      "sig",
      "signature",
      "x-amz-signature",
      "x-amz-credential",
      "x-amz-security-token",
      "auth"
    ],
    "ENDPOINT_ID_SEGMENT_RES": [
      "^\\d+$",
      "^[0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}$",
      "^[0-9a-fA-F]{24}$",
      "^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,}$"
    ],
    "REDACTED": "[REDACTED]",
    "TOKEN_SHAPES": [
      "gh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}",
      "github_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]{20,}",
      "glpat-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,}",
      "xox[abprs]-[A-Za-z0-9-]{10,}",
      "sk-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}",
      "AKIA[A-Z0-9]{16}",
      "[A-Za-z0-9+/=_-]{40,}"
    ],
    "JSON_DEPTH_MAX": 10,
    "UNNAMED_KEYS": "_unnamed_keys",
    "ERROR_MAX": 200,
    "JSON_PAIR_RE": "\"((?:[^\"\\\\\\r\\n]|\\\\.){1,128})\"(\\s*:\\s*)(?:\"(?:[^\"\\\\]|\\\\.)*(?:\"|$(?![\\s\\S]))|-?[0-9][0-9.eE+-]*)",
    "FORM_PAIR_RE": "(?<![A-Za-z0-9_.-])([A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_.-]{0,127})=([^&\\s\\\"',;]+)",
    "URL_PARTS_RE": "\\A(?:([A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9+.-]*):)?(?://([^/?#]*))?([^?#]*)(?:\\?([^#]*))?(?:#[\\s\\S]*)?\\Z"
  },
  "cases": [
    {
